# Frontend settings for PRODUCTION builds. Set these in your frontend host's
# dashboard (e.g. Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables), or copy to
# client/.env.production before running "npm run build". Never put secrets here:
# everything starting with VITE_ ends up in the public JavaScript.
#
# Option A, Vercel (recommended), and option B, one Render service:
#   keep /api, because the website and the API share one address. Nothing to set.
# Option C, website on another host (e.g. Netlify):
#   with the /api proxy from netlify.toml, keep /api as well;
#   calling the API directly instead:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://YOUR-ACTUAL-BACKEND-DOMAIN/api
#   (and on the server: CLIENT_ORIGIN=<website address>, COOKIE_SAME_SITE=none)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
